    "boisterous": {
      "word": "BOISTEROUS",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Rough or rude; unbending; unyielding; strong; powerful. [Obs.] \"Boisterous sword.\" \"Boisterous hand.\" Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Exhibiting tumultuous violence and fury; acting with noisy turbulence; violent; rough; stormy. The waters swell before a boisterous storm. Shak. The brute and boisterous force of violent men. Milton.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Noisy; rough; turbulent; as, boisterous mirth; boisterous behavior. I like not that loud, boisterous man. Addison.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vehement; excessive. [R.] The heat becomes too powerful and boisterous for them. Woodward. noisy; impetuous; vehement.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        }
      ],
